  ways to repurpose containers or  something like that and the thumbnail  was horrible that should be an  indication of how great that video is  but it was like my voice was shaky you  could tell that i was nervous i didn't  even have any b-roll because i didn't  know what the heck that was or how to do  it so it's just me talking in this very  monotone voice  i cringe just thinking about it however  i'm also really incredibly proud because  i did it i did the thing that i was  afraid to do and this is the first  lesson that i want to share with you  cast the stone  do it cast the stone i love mother  teresa's famous quote i alone cannot  change the world but i can cast a stone  across the waters to create many ripples  so ask yourself what is that thing that  you've been wanting to do could it be  that voice that's telling you to  audition for that play to start singing  lessons or start your own youtube  channel  ignore the excuses in your head and just  take the first step and don't think of  this project as a whole when my husband  and i started thinking about how we  would finish the house or thinking about  the completion we immediately began to  feel overwhelmed but when we broke it  down into tiny pieces like for example  this week we will lay flooring it  suddenly became obtainable and then we  started to feel a sense of satisfaction  as we actually achieve those small goals  so that would be my first lesson to you  is don't focus on the big picture ask  yourself what's one thing that you can  do right now to get started  and do it  the first step is the hardest it's where  you meet the most resistance so  congratulate yourself and the fact that  you actually did it  even if the end result makes you cringe  like me in that first video but hey at  least you did it it's better than not  having tried at all if you feel a lot of  pushback or resistance to starting your  goals two books that have been very  helpful to me have been atomic habits by  james clear a