d or destroyed you can choose  to use your energy on dwelling on the  past worrying about the future worrying  about people accepting you or whether or  not things will work out or you can  choose to let all of that go and focus  that energy on actually accomplishing  your goals and your dreams the moment i  posted that video was like a wall had  just come down because i no longer had  to spend energy trying to hide an aspect  of myself and who i was and it gave me a  sense of freedom  know your why  one of the books that has really  resonated with me is start with why by  simon sinek and a narrative that has  really stuck with me is a little  something like this if i were to pay you  money to walk from the top of one  building to another across a rope you  would likely look at me and say heck no  i'm not risking my life for that but if  i told you that on the other building is  your child and this building is about to  fall down or burn down then you may be  more likely to actually do it and go  across to try to save your child  but why  the action is the same you're still  walking from the top of one building to  another across a rope it's because your  why changed the moment we put a child on  that other side of the building and that  building's gonna burn down or it's gonna  fall down then the story changes your  motivation and your reason why changes  having a baby who still wakes me up  almost every single night a toddler and  a full-time job i have to get up at five  in the morning to be able to research  video topics script edit film etc and  having my why  becomes very important to be able to get  out of the bed in the morning because if  it was about what i wanted  i would say i'm going back to bed now i  will say that balance is something that  i find very important so i am not  telling you to overwork yourself because  you have to make your health a priority  but rather to try to ask yourself the  question what motivates me are you  motivated by fame are